    "teach_2": {
      "id": "teach_2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A product can also pair with a linear clue.\n\nSuppose Anil×Nita = 240 and twice Nita is 4 more than Anil.\nLet Anil=x, so Nita=240/x.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_2_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_2_step": {
      "id": "teach_2_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Use the second clue:\n2(240/x) − x = 4\n480 − x² = 4x\nx² + 4x − 480 = 0\n(x+24)(x−20)=0\n\nSo Anil=20 and Nita=12. Check: 20×12=240 and 2×12 is 4 more than 20. The negative root cannot represent an age.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_2"
        }
      ]
    },
